course: dictionary
lesson: 2095
title: Contestant: a person who takes part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A contestant is a person who takes part in a competition, quiz or game show and tries to win. In «the next contestant», the word means the next person to take part. You can see the same idea in «game show contestant» and «each contestant».
explain: Look for clues around the word. «A good viewer enjoys the show and still remembers: the contestants are real people who deserve the kindness you would show a classmate.» Viewers watch the show, but contestants are the people taking part in it, so they are the ones trying to win.
explain: Contestants are not only on TV. In a spelling bee, each child who stands up to spell a word is a contestant. Ask yourself: who is trying to win? That person is the contestant.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A contestant is a person who takes part in a competition, quiz or game show and tries to win.
fact: Contestants answer questions or perform to win prizes.
fact: Phrases to know: «the next contestant», «game show contestant», «each contestant».
fact: Contestants are real people, so treat them with the same kindness you would show a classmate.
exercise: «The next contestant walked onto the stage.» What is a contestant? | A camera on a stand | A host who asks the questions | A prize for the winner | *A person who takes part in a competition and tries to win
exercise: In a spelling bee, who is the contestant? | The parent who films the event | The teacher who reads out the words | *The child who stands up to spell | The judge who sits at the back
exercise: Which person is a contestant? | A child watching a quiz at home on the sofa | A teacher reading the questions aloud | A man who sells tickets at the door | *A child taking part in a talent show to win a prize
test: «Each contestant was nervous before the quiz began.» What does contestant mean? | A kind of prize | The person writing the quiz questions | The place where the quiz is held | *A person who takes part in a competition and tries to win
test: Which phrase means the person who goes on next? | *the next contestant | the quiz master | the last winner | the empty stage
exam: «Most contestants go back to normal life after the show.» Why are they called contestants here? | They are the viewers who watched at home | *They took part in a show and tried to win | They are the people who sell the tickets | The show's hosts and judges
